-\frac{2x}{4} + y = -\frac{9}{4} \implies y = \frac{1}{2}x - \frac{9}{4}
\] From this, we can see that the slope $m$ of the line is $\frac{1}{2}$. Since parallel lines have the same slope, the slope of any line parallel to $2x - 4y = 9$ is also $\frac{1}{2}$. </think> <answer> $\frac{1}{2}$ </answer>

